WEBVTT

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:22.760
Spider-Man does whatever a spider can, spins a web any size, catches thieves just like flies, look out, here comes the Spider-Man.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:29.640
Is he strong? Listen bud, he's got radioactive blood, can you swing?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.920
From a thread, take a look, overhead

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.040
Hey there, there goes a Spider-Man

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:41.480
The chill of night, the scene of a crime

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:46.290
Like a streak of night, he arrives just in time

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:51.070
Spider-Man, Spider-Man, friendly neighborhood Spider-Man

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.320
Wealth and fame, he's ignored

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.560
Action is his reward to him

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.730
Life is a great big bang up wherever

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:02.940
The Spider-Man

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.400
I've been robbed!

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.120
Hang on, Louie.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.920
The clock strikes, we strike.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.960
Neat haul, huh, Dr. Coon?

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.730
My midnight hulls are always neat, aren't they, Garth?

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:37.650
Better put the ice on ice.

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:44.600
What? Front for hot ice.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:49.270
Yes, we will set the nuclear thermostat for absolute zero.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:57.780
In this super-frosted form, it will be impossible to discern our hot ice from the ordinary variety.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.980
Then, write under the note...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.600
of international customs, we will make the customary shipments

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.650
at customary province.

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:10.230
Yeah, Doc, a real gem of a set-up.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.390
I wonder what we'll get for this.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:15.570
About 10 to 20 years, I'd guess.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:16.970
Spider-Man!

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.010
Of course, there's always time off for good behavior.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:23.550
And you fellas are going to behave, aren't you?

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.150
Oh, yeah? I'll get this.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.250
Sit down.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.180
Garth, I suggest you take this gentleman's advice.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:35.740
But, God!

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:38.970
It appears he has us at the advantage.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:42.180
I bow to your good sense.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.200
Just what the doctor ordered.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:56.020
Buy him up.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.970
If you can hear me, wet wonder, in your...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.360
your semi-stupor.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.260
Know then that I prescribe for your meddlesome intrusion

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.780
this chilling thing.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:09.950
Leave here.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:13.650
The temperature will drop to minus 459 degrees,

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.210
absolute zero.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:20.500
Bad temperature, all your body's molecular motion

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.000
will suddenly cease.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:29.350
And since this refrigeration unit is nuclear-powered,

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:33.950
You will probably keep forever on ice.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:42.150
And you have heard, have you not, webbed wonder,

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:46.600
of the incredible delusions that come on the mind as it numb.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:52.520
People imagine all sorts of things before their frozen doom.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.780
Now you shall see.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:57.740
Dream.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:20.020
Hard to get leverage, weak, but I've got to get loose before the cold takes over.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:24.520
Mercury's dropping fast toward absolute zero.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:04.040
Thank you.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:31.960
It sure feels good to move again.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:35.980
I guess the nuclear power ran down in record time.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:48.790
How long have I been sleeping?

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:50.190
All this wasn't here before.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.490
I would have remembered when I came in.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:54.860
And how long ago was that?

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:29.720
Good grief! Beasts have taken over, but how?

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:40.620
Why, man?

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:02.110
Got to keep my senses, got to keep my head.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.830
Despite all that's going on, however it happened

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.840
and however I got here, I've got to survive.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.520
Now, get crackin'.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.670
It's set for a bring-down.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.100
Say, stick around, I may use you.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:34.470
You

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:18.450
I wonder what...

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.670
Hey, what's this?

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:12.190
One chance.

00:12:02.972 --> 00:12:04.152
tie the final knot.

00:12:04.444 --> 00:12:06.444
You

00:12:14.716 --> 00:12:15.936
The bigger they come,

00:13:04.252 --> 00:13:05.312
like more trouble.

00:13:05.852 --> 00:13:07.792
And here it comes.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:34.620
Yes, but who are you?

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:39.640
The Ice Man. I just stopped in off my regular run to pick up a load.

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:42.260
Figured I'd get caught up on my work, you know.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:46.470
Lucky for you, I did. Boy, it sure was cold in here.

00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:50.880
I know my ice, and I figure you must have been like that at least 24 hours.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.020
24 hours?

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:58.880
Yeah, you was almost a goner. Somebody turned to the thermostat way down to absolute zero.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:16:59.980
Boy, he...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.040
He must be some kind of a nut.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:04.720
No, he's a mighty cool customer.

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:07.890
Well, in your racket, I guess you meet all kinds.

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:10.150
You say this isn't your regular run.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:13.130
No, I'm not supposed to pick up the ice here till morning.

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:16.530
But I got a little ahead and I figured, what's the harm?

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:18.580
You sure figured right.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:22.060
Like I was saying, but who could have froze you up like that?

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.620
They obviously planned to do away with me

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:28.300
before the Iceman got here.

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:29.970
So, I guess...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.060
I can soon expect another visit from the crooked Dr. Cool.

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:35.500
What time is it?

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:37.460
It's midnight.

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:21.270
I think I'll get set for a hot reception.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.100
This time you'll get the cooler.

00:18:45.590 --> 00:18:46.790
Fireman! No!

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:15.280
I'll have to hand it to you, Spider-Man.

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:17.810
They sure were a pair of slippery characters.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:19.150
How did you handle it?

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:20.430
I don't know.

00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:24.290
I guess you could say I just kept my cool.

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:53.680
Spider-Man does whatever a spider can, spins a web any size, catches thieves just like flies, look out, here comes the Spider-Man.

00:20:55.570 --> 00:20:59.570
Is he strong? Listen bud, he's got radioactive blood.

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:29.970
Swing Thread, take a look, overhead, hey there, there goes a Spider-Man, cheer the scene of the streets, he arrives just in time, Spider-Man, Spider-Man, friendly neighborhood Spider-Man, wealth and fame, he's ignored, action is his reward to him, life is a great big bang, a

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:34.060
Where there's a hat, you'll find the Spider-Man.
